## Quick checklist – did you miss anything?

| ✅ | Item |
|---|------|
| **✅** | `MapLibre.setModuleProvider(...)` is called **before** the first `MapView`/`MapLibreMap` is instantiated. |
| **✅** | Your `Vault.decryptTile(z, x, y)` returns **exactly** the raw MVT bytes (no extra wrapper, no compression beyond what the source expects). |
| **✅** | You return **200** with a non-null body; otherwise the layer will be dropped silently. |
| **✅** | If you need caching, you can add `Cache-Control`/`ETag` headers in the `onResponse` call – MapLibre will store the tile in its internal cache. |
| **✅** | For debugging, enable MapLibre logging (`MapLibre.setLogLevel(MapLibre.LOG_LEVEL_DEBUG)`) – you’ll see lines like `[HttpRequest] request: vault://tiles/12/3456/7890`. |
| **❌** | Do **not** try to use `FileSource.setResourceTransform` – it only rewrites URLs, it cannot supply raw bytes. |
| **❌** | Do **not** look for `MapLibre.addProtocol` – it does not exist on Native. |
